{{Quote|By that time, there had been a new member added to the crew of the ''Ghost''&mdash;Spectre-7, Jacen Syndulla. Born to fly, just like his mother. And, well, we all know what his father was like.|Sabine Wren|<ref name="Family Reunion – and Farewell" />}}
'''Jacen Syndulla''' was a [[Force-sensitive]] [[Gender|male]] [[human]]-[[Twi'lek]] [[hybrid]] who was [[Reproduction|born]] during the time of the [[Galactic Civil War]]. He was the son of [[General]] [[Hera Syndulla]] and the late [[Jedi Knight]] [[Kanan Jarrus]], and the grandson of Twi'lek revolutionary leader [[Cham Syndulla]].

==Biography==
===Birth and early years===
{{Quote|It's why we need to work for it. Everything we're doing right now&hellip;it's for the New Republic, not for us. But I've got a family. I've got a son who needs me, a homeworld I haven't seen in too long. I've got people who I care about&mdash;I want to live for ''them'' awhile, instead of the galaxy.|Hera Syndulla, to [[Nath Tensent]]|<ref name="Victory's Price">''[[Victory's Price: An Alphabet Squadron Novel]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Jacen_Syndulla.jpg|left|thumb|200px|Jacen Syndulla following the end of the Galactic Civil War.]]
Jacen Syndulla was [[Reproduction|born]] to [[General]] [[Hera Syndulla]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> in [[1 BBY]].<ref name="Birth year" /> His [[Parent|father]] was [[Jedi Knight]] [[Kanan Jarrus]],<ref name="Family Reunion – and Farewell" /> who was [[Death|killed]] in combat, before Syndulla was born, against the [[Galactic Empire]] while [[Rescue of Hera Syndulla (Lothal)|saving]] Hera and their [[Spectres|crew]] shortly before [[Liberation of Lothal|Lothal's liberation]].<ref name="Jedi Night">{{Rebels|Jedi Night}}</ref> He was the grandson of [[Twi'lek]] freedom fighter [[Cham Syndulla]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> a legendary veteran of the [[Clone Wars]] and the [[Ryloth Insurgency|fight against]] the Empire.<ref name="Homecoming">{{Rebels|Homecoming}}</ref>

Syndulla grew up during the [[Galactic Civil War]], which his mother fought in for the Rebel Alliance.<ref name="Family Reunion – and Farewell" /> By the [[time]] the Empire was shattered in [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> during the [[Battle of Endor]], the young Syndulla was already considered a member of his mother's crew on the [[starship]] ''[[Ghost]]'' and was given the [[callsign]] Spectre 7.<ref name="Family Reunion – and Farewell" /> Although Syndulla grew up never knowing his father, he was nonetheless surrounded by love from the people he considered family, including the [[droid]] [[C1-10P]] or "Chopper."<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> Chopper, who was a companion to his mother since her childhood,<ref name="Homecoming" /> became a close and constant companion to Syndulla. Despite the aged [[Astromech droid|astromech's]] usually cantankerous personality, being around the young boy brought out his playful side.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

By [[5 ABY]], Jacen and Hera were separated as his mother participated in the final stretch of the Galactic Civil War, including the [[Battle of Jakku]] where she had a near-death experience and thought of Jacen during what she believed to be her last moments.<ref name="Victory's Price" />

===New Republic===
{{Quote|I wanna be a Jedi.''"<br />"''Yeah, I know you do, Jacen.|Jacen Syndulla and Hera Syndulla|<ref name="Part 3" />}}
[[File:Hera_and_Jacen_after_a_New_Republic_meeting.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Jacen talking to his mother after her meeting.]]
Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Ahsoka series date">{{AhsokaSeriesDate}}</ref> Jacen accompanied his mother when she went to speak with the [[New Republic]] Senate Committee, staying with Chopper while Hera attended the meeting via hologram, requesting approval to lead a task force to the [[Denab system]] for an investigation following an incident involving [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] loyalists that may indicate the return of [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]]. While his mom was in the meeting, Chopper told Jacen that "Aunt [[Sabine Wren|Sabine]]" was training under [[Ahsoka Tano]] to become a [[Jedi]]. After Hera got out of her meeting, Jacen told his mom that he also wanted to be a Jedi.<ref name="Part 3" />

Following an urgent call that his mother received from [[Huyang]], requesting assistance for Wren and Tano on [[Seatos]], Jacen and Chopper went with her aboard the ''Ghost''. Along with five [[T-65B X-wing starfighter]]s flown by [[Captain]] [[Carson Teva]] and [[Lieutenant]]s [[Baysee]], [[Mowaat]], [[Jensu]], and [[Lander (individual)|Lander]], the [[Hera Syndulla's fleet|fleet]] jumped into [[hyperspace]] at Hera's command as Jacen pulled the hyperdrive lever.<ref name="Part 4">{{Ahsoka|Part Four: Fallen Jedi}}</ref>

Arriving at Seatos, Jacen and his mother narrowly avoided the ''[[Eye of Sion]]''{{'s}} path of destruction as it jumped to hyperspace.<ref name="Part 4" /> Landing on the planet's surface, the two immediately sensed that something was off, with both Ahsoka and Sabine having disappeared without explanation. Unbeknownst to them, Ahsoka had been cast into the waters around the reflex point henge and was in the midst of a near death experience within the mysterious [[World Between Worlds]]. Through the Force, Jacen sensed her presence, and helped Huyang and his mother find and rescue the wayward Jedi from the sea. Following her recovery, Jacen and Ahsoka shared a warm reunion before she and Huyang made their own hyperspace jump in pursuit of the ''Eye of Sion'' with the help of a flock of [[Purrgil]]. Jacen watched with wonder from the ''Ghost'' as the immense creatures vanished with a brilliant flash of light into the vastness of space.<ref name="Part 5">{{Ahsoka|Part Five: Shadow Warrior}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|How's young Jacen?''"<br />"''Fine, Chancellor, in fact he's on board. Somewhere.''"<br />"''[chuckles] Causing trouble with Chopper, no doubt.''"<br />"''Most likely.|[[Chancellor (New Republic)|Chancellor]] Mon Mothma and Hera Syndulla on Jacen|<ref name="Part 3" />}}
Jacen Syndulla was a [[Gender|male]] [[hybrid]], born to a [[human]] father and a Twi'lek mother. He had mostly human features, though his [[Color|green]] [[hair]] was similar to his mother's green skin, and the tips of his [[ear]]s and his eyelashes were also green.<ref name="Family Reunion – and Farewell" /> By the time of the New Republic Era, Jacen was 1.42 [[meter]]s tall.<ref name="Databank" />

The blend of his exceptional parents,<ref name="Databank" /> the boy showed aptitude as a [[pilot]] at a young age,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> and Hera's old friend and crew member, [[Sabine Wren]], recognized that Syndulla was born to fly, just like his mother. He also had blue [[eye]]s<ref name="Family Reunion – and Farewell" /> and tan skin.<ref name="Part 3" /> Jacen had a close relationship with Chopper, who became his companion while his mother was away,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> with the two gaining a reputation for causing trouble when left together, as noted by [[Mon Mothma]]. Jacen also wished to become a Jedi, like his father before him.<ref name="Part 3" /> He also has a close relationship with the rest of the [[Spectres|Spectre crew]] as well as [[Ahsoka Tano|Ahsoka]], referring to Sabine as 'Aunt Wren'. 

==Powers and abilities==
{{Quote|Jacen has abilities. His father, Kanan Jarrus, was a Jedi.|Huyang to Carson Teva|<ref name="Part 5" />}}
Like his father, Jacen was Force-sensitive, his strong connection to [[the Force]] allowed him to sense Ahsoka Tano duel with her former Master Anakin Skywalker in the World Between Worlds, hearing the lightsabers clash, which allowed the New Republic fleet to find Tano.<ref name="Part 5" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|It seemed, in a very small way, naming him 'Jacen' was a way to honor the expanded universe character of Jacen Solo who just really isn't there anymore as the timelines have changed. I thought that's a little bit of a wink to people that I know that was an important character. And maybe, in some way, that lives on through this character. I don't know yet.|Dave Filoni on Jacen Syndulla's namesake|<ref name="Filoni io9">{{WebCite|url=https://io9.gizmodo.com/lucasfilm-creatives-are-very-interested-in-that-new-sta-1823646768|text=Lucasfilm Creatives Are Very Interested in That New ''Star Wars Rebels'' Character|author=Lussier, Germain|date=2018-03-09|work=io9|archivedate=20200128172304}}</ref>}}
[[File:Jacen_concept_art.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Concept art for Jacen Syndulla]]
Jacen Syndulla was introduced in the epilogue of "[[Family Reunion – and Farewell]]," the series finale of ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''.<ref name="Family Reunion – and Farewell" /> His first name, Jacen, was inspired by [[Darth Caedus|Jacen Solo]], the son of [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa Solo]] and [[Han Solo/Legends|Han Solo]] in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity.<ref name="SW.com Twitter">{{Twitter|starwars|status/970856627401211904|''[[Star Wars]]''|date=2018-03-01|quote=Spelled exactly like you're hoping it is. 😉 #StarWarsRebels|archivefile=File:Jacen Syndulla Star Wars Twitter.png|archivedate=20191128012949}}</ref>

The decision to introduce Jacen Syndulla in the series finale was one that executive producer [[Dave Filoni]] had been thinking of throughout production on the [[Star Wars Rebels Season Four|fourth season]]. He initially only shared his idea with [[Kiri Hart]], the head of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]], who was supportive of the character's introduction. Filoni deliberately chose the name Jacen as a way of honoring the character of Jacen Solo and his importance in the stories of ''[[Star Wars]]'' Legends.<ref name="Filoni io9" /> Voice actress [[Vanessa Marshall]], however, was unaware of Hera's pregnancy with Jacen when she recorded the final episode, only discovering it during a fan screening.<ref name="Vanessa Fandom">{{YouTube|video=CvF4EQ_LqYQ|text='Star Wars: Rebels' Star Talks Hera Sydulla's Fate, Return of 'Clone Wars'|channel=channel/UC988qTQImTjO7lUdPfYabgQ|name=FANDOM|quote=I never expected her "spoiler alert" for her to have a child. That, that shocked me in the moment live at the fan screening. I had no idea in the epilogue. That was pretty amazing.}}</ref>

At Dragon Con [[2018]], when asked by [[StarWars.com]] writer [[Bria LaVorgna]] about when Jacen was conceived, ''Rebels'' writer [[Henry Gilroy]] stated that Jacen may have been conceived during the episode "[[Kindred]]," describing the scene where Hera finds Kanan meditating out in the fields only for the scene to be cut short with a time cut.<ref name="DragonCon2018">{{WebCite|url=https://thewookieegunner.com/2018/09/08/star-wars-animation-panels-highlights-dragon-con/#more-17162|text=Highlights of the 'Star Wars' Animation Panels at Dragon Con 2018|author=Macias, Johnamarie|date=2018-09-08|quote=Bria LaVorgna brought up the question of when Jacen Syndulla was conceived. Gilroy described a scene from the episode "Kindred," where Hera finds Kanan meditating out in the fields. He said there was a time-cut or dissolve after that and "a lot of things can happen in a dissolve."|nobackup=1}}</ref> However, this has not been stated in any [[canon]] source.

Though Filoni says he has not given much thought to where the character might go in future stories, many creatives within Lucasfilm have expressed interest in the future of the character since the ''Star Wars Rebels'' finale aired on [[March 5]], 2018.<ref name="Filoni io9" /> Jacen was later revealed to appear in the upcoming ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]'' series via the [[LEGO]] set [[w:c:brickipedia:75357 Ghost & Phantom II|75357 Ghost & Phantom II]]. In the set, the character is depicted with brown hair;<ref name="LEGO Ghost">{{LEGOWeb|url=en-us/product/ghost-phantom-ii-75357|text=Ghost & Phantom II}}</ref> however, the series still depicts him with green hair. He was first depicted in live-action in "[[Part Three: Time to Fly]]," the third episode of ''Ahsoka''. He was portrayed by [[Evan Whitten]].<ref name="Part 3" />

